## Part 2. Viral Sequence Analysis in Galaxy

### Step 1. Set Up Your Galaxy Account

1. Go to **[Galaxy](https://galaxy-main.usegalaxy.org/)**.
2. Register for a free account or log in if you already have one.
3. Create a **new history** by clicking the **+** sign in the upper-right corner.
4. Name your history **Virus Phylogeny**.

### Step 2. Find the Workflow

1. Navigate to **Workflows**.
2. Open the **Curated Workflows** section.
3. Search for **HyPhy: Preprocessing**.
4. Select the workflow.

### Step 3. Upload and Assign Your Files

Use the three files downloaded from NCBI Virus:

| Workflow input | File |
|---|---|
| Annotation file | Reference genome annotations (`.gff3`) |
| Reference FASTA | Complete reference genome (`.fasta`) |
| Viral sequence database | Dataset of viral sequences (`.fasta`) |

Make sure each file is assigned to the correct input.

### Step 4. Run the Workflow

1. Review your input files and workflow settings.
2. Click **Run Workflow**.
3. Monitor the progress in your Galaxy history.
4. Once the workflow finishes, explore the generated output files.
